WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:01.354
- All right, let's see.

00:00:01.354 --> 00:00:03.937
(bouncy music)

00:00:06.710 --> 00:00:09.020
You did not type in anything there.

00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:10.016
Let's do it again.

00:00:10.016 --> 00:00:11.110
- [Joanna Voiceover] Okay,
I'm thinking this scene

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:13.060
needs a bit of explaining.

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:15.880
So you've probably noticed
we're all wearing masks

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:17.200
because well,

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:18.328
- You must now wear a mask.

00:00:18.328 --> 00:00:19.161
- A mask.
- A mask.

00:00:19.161 --> 00:00:19.994
- A mask.
- A mask.

00:00:19.994 --> 00:00:21.097
- [Squeaking Voices] Mask, mask, mask.

00:00:21.097 --> 00:00:22.052
- Everywhere you go.

00:00:22.052 --> 00:00:24.160
- [Joanna Voiceover] But one
slight problem I realized.

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:27.800
Apple's face unlock feature, AKA Face ID,

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:29.390
doesn't let you into your phone

00:00:29.390 --> 00:00:31.920
when a mask is covering
your nose and mouth.

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:32.891
- Mask number one.

00:00:32.891 --> 00:00:33.724
- [Joanna Voiceover] Believe me,

00:00:33.724 --> 00:00:35.311
I've tried many, many masks.

00:00:35.311 --> 00:00:36.144
- This is a handmade mask.

00:00:36.144 --> 00:00:37.500
- [Joanna Voiceover] And tried retraining

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:40.010
the whole system many, many times.

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:41.938
- Nope, not letting me in.

00:00:41.938 --> 00:00:43.670
- [Joanna Voiceover]
That's when I came across.

00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:45.130
- I'm Danielle Baskin.

00:00:45.130 --> 00:00:46.120
- And what do you do?

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:47.450
- I'm a product designer.

00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:49.095
- What are you talking
about with me today?

00:00:49.095 --> 00:00:51.768
(laughter)

00:00:51.768 --> 00:00:52.650
- [Joanna Voiceover] Back in February,

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:55.830
Danielle had the funny idea
to print faces on masks

00:00:55.830 --> 00:00:59.140
because she had heard about
that Face ID and mask issue.

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:02.190
There was just one slight
problem with those.

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:05.380
- It turns out though that
Face ID actually uses depth

00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:08.180
instead of an image, so
I ended up making a mask

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:10.600
that actually has a contour of your face

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:12.010
that can work with Face ID.

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:13.066
- And does that work?

00:01:13.066 --> 00:01:14.507
- Yes, it works.

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:17.060
- [Joanna Voiceover] I had
to see it to believe it.

00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:19.430
And since I'm sheltering
in place in New Jersey

00:01:19.430 --> 00:01:21.830
and Danielle is in San Francisco,

00:01:21.830 --> 00:01:24.610
I made her demonstrate it via video chat,

00:01:24.610 --> 00:01:25.770
a lot.

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:27.420
I even made her get out a mirror

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:29.670
to make sure I wasn't being played.

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:30.503
- Is this good?

00:01:30.503 --> 00:01:31.680
- That's way better.

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:34.958
(bright music)

00:01:34.958 --> 00:01:36.653
Welp, I believe you now.

00:01:36.653 --> 00:01:37.960
- [Joanna Voiceover] So
this mask isn't exactly

00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:38.920
easy to make.

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:42.280
First, Danielle had to make a
clay form of a nose and mouth.

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:43.600
It wasn't even hers.

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:45.270
Then she made a plastic shell

00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:47.390
using a vacuum former machine.

00:01:47.390 --> 00:01:49.530
When the mask was ready,
she enrolled it as an

00:01:49.530 --> 00:01:53.800
alternate appearance in the
Face ID settings on her iPhone.

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:56.847
Apple said in a statement,
"Face ID is designed to work

00:01:56.847 --> 00:01:59.417
"with your eyes, nose, and mouth visible.

00:01:59.417 --> 00:02:01.827
"Users can still unlock
their devices while

00:02:01.827 --> 00:02:04.620
"wearing a mask by
entering their passcode."

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:07.600
When I tried to enroll my
face using an N-95 mask

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:09.690
and these various other cloth masks,

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:10.980
- Mask number two,

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:11.890
three,

00:02:11.890 --> 00:02:12.723
four.

00:02:12.723 --> 00:02:13.556
- [Joanna Voiceover] I got an error saying

00:02:13.556 --> 00:02:14.900
my face was obstructed.

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:18.120
But with Danielle's mask the
true depth camera on the iPhone

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:20.810
and the Face ID software,
appears to recognize

00:02:20.810 --> 00:02:22.870
the geometry of the face.

00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:25.800
In fact, it even works
when she has sunglasses on.

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:26.633
- Okay, ready?

00:02:26.633 --> 00:02:27.466
- [Joanna] Yup.

00:02:30.130 --> 00:02:30.963
Wow.

00:02:30.963 --> 00:02:31.990
- [Joanna Voiceover] This
is also different from what

00:02:31.990 --> 00:02:33.270
many have tried to do.

00:02:33.270 --> 00:02:35.080
Okay, fine, I tried to do.

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:36.420
By creating a mask of someone

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:38.500
and then attempting to trick the phone,

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:39.880
this isn't trickery.

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:43.230
It requires you enroll the
mask as one of your faces.

00:02:43.230 --> 00:02:45.960
- Are you planing to make
these and sell these?

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:46.830
What's the plan?

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:49.870
- No time soon. I mean, I'm
not, there's a shortage of PPE,

00:02:49.870 --> 00:02:54.820
so I would not capitalize
on making any masks.

00:02:54.820 --> 00:02:57.720
If there is a value to
making these for people

00:02:57.720 --> 00:03:00.447
that work in hospitals, I'm
interested in developing it.

00:03:00.447 --> 00:03:01.950
- [Joanna Voiceover] So
yeah, you're not getting

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:04.870
one of these soon, which
leaves you with two options.

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:07.980
Keep trying to get Face ID
to like your current mask.

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:10.047
- Look like some sort
of bird in this mask.

00:03:10.047 --> 00:03:11.820
- [Joanna Voiceover] Or type your password

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:13.580
over and over and over.

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:15.100
Yes, with gloves on,

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:18.100
which I confirm did not
require any special clay molds

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:19.905
or special machinery.

00:03:19.905 --> 00:03:24.262
(upbeat music)
(caw-caws like a bird)

